in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @magic/contract
in @magic/audit

# @magic/mechanism — the matter-hidden encapsulation species. Dual
# of @magic/surface; closes the gauge ↔ matter symmetry the @magic
# substrate-decl named at family-root.
#
# Tick 13 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 12's residue:
# audit's bilateral predicate `audited(c)` declared at @magic/audit
# but no consumer that exercises the discipline (parallel to
# contract.invariant_preserved which surface.mirror just consumed).
#
# CRQ: who's the consumer of @magic/audit's bilateral predicate?
# Without one, the audit discipline is paint at audit altitude —
# same failure mode Seam caught at tick 11.
#
# Answer: @magic/mechanism's `unseal` action. The substrate-pull-
# correct controlled disclosure of matter REQUIRES the contract to
# have been audited before the mechanism reveals its content. That's
# the SECOND non-decorative `requires` clause in the @magic family,
# composing with audit's predicate as surface composed with contract's.
#
# === The mechanism as matter ===
#
# Per recognition #80, the mechanism IS the matter-hidden trick
# (encapsulated; observer cannot inspect from the gauge alone). Per
# recognition #76 (gauge/matter altitude-portable; research-promoted),
# matter expands at three altitudes (splinter/prism-instance/sheaf).
# This species declares the substrate's @magic-altitude matter
# encapsulation primitive.
#
# At Clarke's-law altitude: the mechanism IS the sleight, the
# preparation, the confederate, the mechanical aid. The audience
# cannot inspect; the trick stays hidden behind the surface.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `mechanism_invariant` carrier (substrate-typed invariant the
#   matter side commits to, distinct from surface_invariant which
#   names gauge-altitude commitments).
# - `seal(content) -> magic_mechanism`: matter encapsulation — takes
#   substrate-typed content and produces an encapsulated mechanism
#   whose interior is opaque to the gauge.
# - `unseal(m, key) -> ref`: controlled disclosure of mechanism
#   content. Requires `audited(c)` per the contract that holds this
#   mechanism — the SECOND non-decorative `requires` clause in
#   @magic, consuming @magic/audit's bilateral predicate.
# - `mechanism_intact` action: bilateral verdict that the matter has
#   not been tampered with since seal. Composes with audit_record's
#   witness to provide tamper-evidence.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   matter field (physics)      Yang-Mills 1954 (matter field acting
#                               on by gauge symmetry). @magic/mechanism
#                               IS the matter-side substrate-decl.
#   capability-based security   Dennis-Van Horn 1966; Levy 1984
#                               (Capability-Based Computer Systems).
#                               The seal/unseal sequence with
#                               capability-key access. @magic/mechanism's
#                               seal+unseal lifts this discipline to
#                               substrate altitude.
#   sealed-trait pattern        Rust's `sealed` trait pattern + the
#                               OCaml functor's hidden representation.
#                               The matter-side encapsulation discipline
#                               at programming altitude.
#   stage-magic apparatus       The mechanism behind the trick — the
#                               cards in the sleeve, the loaded die,
#                               the prepared box. The cultural-practice
#                               ancestor of matter-side encapsulation.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-80-magic-as-form-
#               process-substrate-decl.md;
#               docs/specs/cascade-recognition-76-through-80-
#               canonical-spec.md (Mara's canonical spec landed in
#               this tick's bundled commit).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; mechanism_intact IS the
#                       alignment check at the matter altitude;
#                       complements surface_honest at the gauge
#                       altitude landed at tick 12),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (mechanism_invariant
#                       and action signatures typed; seal/unseal
#                       respect the encapsulation discipline).
# Related shards: magic.mirror (the family-root; magic_mechanism and
#                  magic_invariant declared here),
#                 magic/contract.mirror (the contract that holds
#                  this mechanism; mechanism_intact composes with
#                  the contract via the audit altitude),
#                 magic/audit.mirror (audit's bilateral predicate
#                  `audited(c)` consumed by unseal; the second
#                  non-decorative `requires` clause in @magic),
#                 magic/surface.mirror (the gauge-side dual; together
#                  these two species complete the @magic family's
#                  symmetry).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/magic/mechanism.mirror` declares `@magic/mechanism` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/physics/yang-mills-1954
source @arxiv/security/dennis-van-horn-1966

prism @magic/mechanism {
  focus mechanism
  project mechanism
  split mechanism
  shift mechanism
  settle mechanism
}

# === mechanism_invariant carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming a specific
# invariant the mechanism commits to upholding at the matter
# altitude. Distinct from surface_invariant (gauge-side commitments)
# and magic_invariant (contract-level commitments) by being scoped
# to mechanism-altitude properties: what the matter encapsulation
# preserves regardless of what the surface presents.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type mechanism_invariant = ref

# === seal action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that takes substrate-typed content
# and produces an encapsulated mechanism. The matter encapsulation
# primitive: after seal, the content is opaque to the gauge; only
# unseal (with proper audit) can re-expose it.
#
# At capability-security altitude: seal IS the operation that converts
# data into an opaque capability; the only way to recover the data
# is via unseal with the matching audit.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
seal(content: ref) -> magic_mechanism { \ }

# === unseal action ===
#
# THE SECOND NON-DECORATIVE `requires` CLAUSE CONSUMER per tick 13.
# The substrate-vocabulary action that exposes the encapsulated
# content of a mechanism, but ONLY when the contract that holds the
# mechanism has been audited.
#
# requires audited(c): the substrate-political bilateral commitment
# that the contract holding this mechanism has been verified. The
# audit's predicate at @magic/audit finally has its first consumer
# (parallel to invariant_preserved gaining its consumer at
# surface.mirror tick 12).
#
# At capability-security altitude: unseal IS the controlled
# disclosure — the audit IS the capability check that permits
# access. Without audit, the matter stays opaque.
#
# At Clarke's-law altitude: unseal IS the magician's reveal at the
# end of the trick — the mechanism becomes visible, but only after
# the contract has been honored (the trick completes per its terms).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
unseal(m: magic_mechanism, c: magic_contract) -> ref
requires audited(c)
{ \ }

# === mechanism_intact action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that verifies the mechanism's
# matter has not been tampered with since seal. Composes with the
# audit_record's witness to provide tamper-evidence.
#
# Returns the substrate's existing verdict carrier (success / partial
# / failure trichotomy). Used by downstream consumers that need
# integrity guarantees beyond the surface-altitude check.
mechanism_intact(m: magic_mechanism) -> verdict { \ }

out @magic/mechanism
out mechanism_invariant
out seal
out unseal
out mechanism_intact
